  "template": {
    "id": 70,
    "name": "Morning Star Pattern",
    "family": "trend",
    "entry_long": "sma(close - open,{p0}) < {p0} and close > open and (close - open) > {p1} * atr(high,low,close,{p1})",
    "exit_long": "close < ema(close,{p2})",
    "stop_loss_pct": "{sl}",
    "take_profit_pct": null,
    "notes": "The three-candle Morning Star is approximated by a net-negative two-bar body stretch (the down candle plus the small middle candle) followed by a strong bullish confirmation body above 0.5xATR(14), since shifted opens are unavailable. The documented StopLossPercent 1 is used; the confirmation-bar-high target is already met at entry, so a short-MA loss stands in for the exit."
  },
